# Provenance for the three per-product Starfleet OpenAPI specs in
# this directory: byoc.yaml, managed.yaml, account.yaml.
# control-plane.json has entirely different provenance, recorded in
# its own section at the BOTTOM of this file.
#
# These three are CAPTURED from the published public contracts, which
# saas serves unauthenticated (saas #1920):
#
#   GET https://api.pgedge.com/{account,byoc,managed}/v1/openapi.json
#
# Each is already filtered to the public, enterprise-maximal surface
# by saas's own GeneratePublicSpec on the way out — enterprise is the
# union of what any tenant can be served, one CLI binary serves every
# tenant, and a verb outside the caller's plan fails with the API's
# own entitlement error. So the capture IS the public contract;
# nothing on this side derives or filters. From 2025 until 2026-09-01
# these files were instead DERIVED from saas source at a pinned sha,
# reproducing that filter locally because nothing public existed —
# that era's procedure, its pins and its measured findings live in
# this file's git history (#199 closed the derivation).
#
# RE-CAPTURE
#
#   make vendor-spec          # capture from production
#   make vendor-spec-check    # fetch and report drift, write nothing
#   make generate             # regenerate the three clients
#
# Then record the capture in the log below: the date, anything that
# changed shape, and whether devapi agreed with prod at capture time.
# devapi serving a DIFFERENT contract than prod is the early warning
# that a change is rolling out; capture only what production serves.
# Never hand-edit a captured spec.
#
# THE CAPTURE IS STILL FAIL-CLOSED, in the tool (cmd/vendorspec):
# every product is validated before any file is written, and the run
# aborts on an `x-pgedge-*` key anywhere in a contract (the upstream
# filter should have removed every marker, so one appearing means
# that filter regressed — do not vendor the regression), on
# `x-go-type-import` (it names a saas-internal package this module
# cannot import, so the generated client would not compile; a bare
# `x-go-type` is expected — it names UUID, which each module's
# api/types.go supplies), and on a path outside the product's own
# namespace. TestVendoredSpecsCarryNoVisibilityMarkers and
# TestVendoredSpecsAreCanonical assert the first and third invariants
# over the committed artefacts too, so a hand edit cannot reintroduce
# either.
#
# The conversion to YAML is the only transformation: yaml.v3 parses
# the served JSON (integers survive as integers), and the encoder
# emits sorted keys at two-space indent, so two captures of the same
# contract are byte-identical regardless of served key order.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT
#
#   * POST /account/v1/invites/{id}/accept — dropped by saas's own
#     public filter (x-pgedge-omit-public upstream). That costs
#     nothing: `starfleet invite accept` cannot work from an API client
#     under any circumstances — saas's edge proxy never sets both an
#     X-User-ID and an X-Client-ID — so the verb refuses locally with
#     exit 5. TestVendoredSpecsOmitPrivateOperations pins it.
#   * /billing/v1 — saas has no billing spec at all; its handlers sit
#     outside the generated server interface. Deliberately GUI-only.
#
# 2026-09-22 — recapture for saas #1968, backup
#   provenance. devapi and prod were compared structurally
#   (sort-keys JSON diff, servers block excluded): byoc and account
#   byte-identical; managed differed by exactly one addition, the
#   optional root-level Backup.purpose string. purpose was NOT yet
#   served by prod at capture time (confirmed with a direct GET
#   against both hosts), so the content was captured from devapi
#   — the one deliberate exception to "capture only what production
#   serves" this file otherwise holds to — and the servers block was
#   hand-restored to https://api.pgedge.com afterward so the vendored
#   file keeps naming the contract customers are actually served
#   (TestVendoredSpecsAreCanonical pins that literal). Recapture from
#   prod once purpose ships there, to confirm the two still agree.
#
#   The devapi/prod comparison above is about purpose specifically;
#   it does not mean this capture's diff against the PREVIOUSLY
#   VENDORED file is purpose-only, because prod itself had drifted
#   since the 2026-09-18 capture. That drift, all present on prod
#   already and unrelated to purpose: two new paths,
#   /managed/v1/databases/{id}/branches/{branch_id}/logs and its
#   /metrics sibling (GetBranchLogs, GetBranchMetrics), neither yet
#   called by any CLI command; a new 404 response added to the two
#   existing database-level operations GetManagedDatabaseLogs and
#   GetManagedDatabaseMetrics; and description-only rewording on five
#   fields covering branch AI-service inheritance (Branch.services,
#   MCPServiceConfig.embedding_api_key, .init_tokens, .init_users, and
#   ServiceConfig.uri) — a branch now mints or inherits these per the
#   reworded text, where the prior wording said none of that.
#
